# Local (private) evaluation scenarios — never commit
# Authored copies for non-public codebases live here; the playbook at
# docs/eval/playbook.md treats them as one of two safe locations.
docs/eval/scenarios/**/local-*.md
docs/eval/scenarios/**/private/
# Veles eval scenarios are private-by-default: only the shipped public files
# under veles/ are trackable. Any other file (a real-repo Layer-2 scenario)
# is ignored even if it lacks the load-bearing `local-` prefix, so a private
# repo's path/scope can never be committed by accident.
docs/eval/scenarios/veles/*
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/qa-plan-from-diff.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/qa-plan-multi-principal.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/qa-plan-export-pdf-regression.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/qa-plan-defect-grounding.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/qa-plan-defect-grounding-markerless.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/TEMPLATE.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/README.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/fixtures/
docs/eval/scenarios/veles/fixtures/*
!docs/eval/scenarios/veles/fixtures/coverage-classes.md
# Zmora eval scenarios are private-by-default too: a live (Layer-2) scenario
# executes against a real running target and may embed private endpoints, DSNs,
# and responses. Only the shipped public files under zmora/ are trackable.
docs/eval/scenarios/zmora/*
!docs/eval/scenarios/zmora/be-discipline.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/zmora/README.md
!docs/eval/scenarios/zmora/TEMPLATE.md
